    fix(scripts): match broken file links only inside URL delimiters
    
    Previously, `find_locations` searched for the bare basename, so it
    matched the first occurrence on the line — which for a markdown link
    like [`docker-compose.yml`](../../docker-compose.yml) is the display
    text, not the URL, causing the wrong column to be reported.
    
    - Use `(?<=\(|")` lookbehind so the pattern only fires inside `(…)`
      (markdown) or `"…"` (HTML src/href), never in link display text
    - Include optional path-prefix segments in the pattern so the full
      relative path (e.g. `../../docker-compose.yml`) is captured as the
      raw link rather than just the basename
    - Remove the now-redundant `prefix_match` post-adjustment logic
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>

